<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George William, Elector of Brandenburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1595–1640</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George William was Elector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> and Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> from 1619 to 1640. Weak and indecisive, he tried to stay out of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War but could not keep Swedish or imperial armies out of his lands, which were devastated. His minister Adam von Schwarzenberg directed policy, and in 1638 he withdrew to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konigsberg">Königsberg</a>. He was the father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-william-elector-of-brandenburg">the Great Elector</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-william-elector-of-brandenburg.jpg" alt="George William, Elector of Brandenburg" width="320" height="633" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mathias Czwiczek · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GeorgWilhelm.1635.Ausschnitt.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
